# .gitattributes — merge-strategy overrides
#
# journal.host-cleanup.md is a prepend-only rolling log (NEWEST ENTRY FIRST —
# see its own header). Every writer inserts at the same anchor point (right
# after the rules block), so two sessions committing around the same time
# collide there even when their entries never actually conflict in content.
# `merge=union` tells git to auto-combine both sides' lines on conflict
# instead of dropping in <<<<<<< markers — always correct here since "keep
# both entries" is the only sane resolution for this file. Ordering may still
# need a manual pass afterward (union doesn't know about "newest first"), but
# that is a markdown tidy-up, not a broken doc landing in shared history.
# Recurred twice same-day (2026-09-22, commits 14e38f6 and 6a32375) before
# this was added.
journal.host-cleanup.md merge=union
